ros-jazzy-legged-rl-tensorrt_3.7.0-2026.11.03.00.28_arm64.changes:
------------------------------------------------------------------

Format: 1.8
Date: Mon, 02 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0000
Source: ros-jazzy-legged-rl-tensorrt
Binary: ros-jazzy-legged-rl-tensorrt
Built-For-Profiles: noudeb
Architecture: arm64
Version: 3.7.0-2026.11.03.00.28
Distribution: noble
Urgency: high
Maintainer: Qiayuan Liao <liaoqiayuan@gmail.com>
Changed-By: Qiayuan Liao <liaoqiayuan@gmail.com>
Description:
 ros-jazzy-legged-rl-tensorrt - TensorRT inference backend for legged_rl_controllers
Changes:
 ros-jazzy-legged-rl-tensorrt (3.7.0-2026.11.03.00.28) noble; urgency=high
 .
   * Add policy.threads and pluggable inference backends with TensorRT
     policy.threads sets ONNX Runtime's intra-op threads, default 1 (the calling thread). Workers sleep between runs
     instead of spinning. On the G1's Orin NX, 4 threads take the encoder + decoder tick from 3.0 ms to 1.5 ms.
     OnnxPolicy uses the first installed legged::InferenceBackend plugin whose init() succeeds on the machine, after
     checking its outputs against ONNX Runtime on a random input, and logs the choice. Without a plugin nothing changes.
     legged_rl_tensorrt runs the policies on an NVIDIA GPU with FP32 engines (TF32 off), mapped host buffers and a CUDA
     graph: 0.92 ms per encoder + decoder tick on the Orin NX. It loads TensorRT at run time and links the CUDA runtime
     statically, so its deb depends on no NVIDIA package, and a machine without TensorRT or a GPU stays on the CPU.
     Engines are built ahead, about 45 s on the Orin NX, with ros2 run legged_rl_tensorrt build_engine <model.onnx> ...,
     next to the models and keyed by model, GPU and TensorRT version; a missing engine fails configure with that command.
     OnnxPolicy's constructor and layout change, so dependent packages must be rebuilt.
     Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <mailto:noreply@anthropic.com>
     Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01A2pd46YwYV5pUbH2WJmrKG
   * Contributors: qiayuanl
   * Add policy.threads and pluggable inference backends with TensorRT
     policy.threads sets ONNX Runtime's intra-op threads, default 1 (the calling thread). Workers sleep between runs
     instead of spinning. On the G1's Orin NX, 4 threads take the encoder + decoder tick from 3.0 ms to 1.5 ms.
     OnnxPolicy uses the first installed legged::InferenceBackend plugin whose init() succeeds on the machine, after
     checking its outputs against ONNX Runtime on a random input, and logs the choice. Without a plugin nothing changes.
     legged_rl_tensorrt runs the policies on an NVIDIA GPU with FP32 engines (TF32 off), mapped host buffers and a CUDA
     graph: 0.92 ms per encoder + decoder tick on the Orin NX. It loads TensorRT at run time and links the CUDA runtime
     statically, so its deb depends on no NVIDIA package, and a machine without TensorRT or a GPU stays on the CPU.
     Engines are built ahead, about 45 s on the Orin NX, with ros2 run legged_rl_tensorrt build_engine <model.onnx> ...,
     next to the models and keyed by model, GPU and TensorRT version; a missing engine fails configure with that command.
     OnnxPolicy's constructor and layout change, so dependent packages must be rebuilt.
     Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <mailto:noreply@anthropic.com>
     Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01A2pd46YwYV5pUbH2WJmrKG
   * Contributors: qiayuanl
